---
import LegalPage from "../../components/LegalPage.astro";
import { COMPANY } from "../../data/company";
import { legalHref } from "../../i18n";
---

<LegalPage lang="en" page="termeni">
  <p>
    These terms apply to the <strong>{COMPANY.domain}</strong> website (the “website”). The website is operated
    by <strong>{COMPANY.name}</strong> (“HoreLink”, “we” or “us”). By using the website, you agree to the terms
    below.
  </p>

  <dl class="fisa">
    <dt>Company name</dt>
    <dd>{COMPANY.name}</dd>
    <dt>Registered office</dt>
    <dd>{COMPANY.address}, Romania</dd>
    <dt>Tax ID (CUI)</dt>
    <dd>{COMPANY.cui}</dd>
    <dt>Trade Register no.</dt>
    <dd>{COMPANY.regCom}</dd>
    <dt>EUID</dt>
    <dd>{COMPANY.euid}</dd>
  </dl>

  <h2 id="the-website">1. What the website is</h2>
  <p>
    The website presents the HoreLink mobile app, which connects hospitality professionals with restaurants,
    bars, hotels, catering companies and event organisers for one-off collaborations. From the website you can
    download the app from Google Play or the App Store and write to us on WhatsApp through the contact form.
  </p>
  <p>No accounts are created, no listings are published and no payments are made on the website.</p>

  <h2 id="the-app">2. The mobile app</h2>
  <p>
    Your account, profile, published events and applications are managed only inside the app. These terms cover
    the website alone. Use of the app is subject to the conditions that apply to the app and to the store you
    download it from (Google Play or the App Store).
  </p>

  <h2 id="information">3. Information on the website</h2>
  <p>
    The texts, screenshots and images on the website are for presentation. Sample events and listings (for
    example “End-of-year corporate gala”) are illustrative and are not real offers. Which events, roles and
    spots are available is shown in the app, depending on what users publish at that time.
  </p>

  <h2 id="acceptable-use">4. Acceptable use</h2>
  <p>When using the website, you agree not to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>attempt unauthorised access to the website, its servers or other people's data;</li>
    <li>disrupt the website, for example through excessive automated traffic or malicious code;</li>
    <li>use the contact form for unsolicited commercial messages or unlawful content.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="intellectual-property">5. Intellectual property</h2>
  <p>
    The HoreLink name, logo, texts, images and website design belong to {COMPANY.name} or are used under a
    licence. You may not copy, modify or use them commercially without our written consent. Google Play is a
    trademark of Google LLC and App Store is a trademark of Apple Inc.
  </p>

  <h2 id="external-links">6. Links to other services</h2>
  <p>
    The website links to Google Play, the App Store and WhatsApp. These services have their own terms and privacy
    policies, for which we are not responsible. Please read them before using those services.
  </p>

  <h2 id="liability">7. Liability</h2>
  <p>
    We do our best to keep the information on the website accurate and up to date, but we cannot guarantee that
    it is error-free or that the website is always available. The website may be temporarily unavailable for
    maintenance or for technical reasons. To the extent permitted by law, we are not liable for indirect damage
    resulting from the use of the website.
  </p>

  <h2 id="personal-data">8. Personal data and cookies</h2>
  <p>
    How we process personal data is explained in our <a href={legalHref("confidentialitate", "en")}>Privacy policy</a>,
    and the cookies we use are listed in our <a href={legalHref("cookies", "en")}>Cookie policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2 id="changes">9. Changes to these terms</h2>
  <p>
    We may update these terms, for example when the website or the law changes. The date of the last update is
    shown at the top of this page. The version published here applies from that date.
  </p>

  <h2 id="governing-law">10. Governing law</h2>
  <p>
    These terms are governed by Romanian law. We will first try to settle any disagreement amicably; if that is
    not possible, the competent courts in Romania have jurisdiction. If you are a consumer, you may also contact
    the Romanian National Authority for Consumer Protection
    (<a href="https://anpc.ro/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">anpc.ro</a>).
  </p>

  <h2 id="contact">11. Contact</h2>
  <p>
    For any question about these terms, write to <a href={`mailto:${COMPANY.email}`}>{COMPANY.email}</a> or call{" "}
    <a href={COMPANY.phoneHref}>+40 {COMPANY.phone.slice(1)}</a>.
  </p>
</LegalPage>
